//? Title: Ladder VAE: Precision Fusion and a Conditional Lower Prior
//? Subtitle: Explicit two-level Gaussian samples, visible Adam and image-free ancestral decoding
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A Ladder VAE combines bottom-up Gaussian evidence with a top-down learned prior by adding
precisions. This report derives that fusion with a hand-checkable example and fits a compact
two-level model on 294 binary known-factor images. It preserves 22 tensors/52,196 parameters,
21 explicit Adam updates, fresh per-epoch Gaussian banks and four-draw validation selection.
Epoch3 is selected. Test negative ELBO is 246.529827 nats/image, comprising NLL234.154285,
lower KL7.508567 and top KL4.866975. Recursive greedy-mean MSE0.073146 is worse than the
fitting mean0.048548. Noise interventions and unfiltered reconstructions/ancestral probabilities
retain the short run's limitations. The model demonstrates precision-fusion inference, not
the paper's full batch-normalized, warmup training recipe or useful semantic disentanglement.
)
\toc

> Bottom-up evidence corrected by a sampled top-down prior

[Sonderby et al.'s Ladder Variational Autoencoders](https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.02282)
combine data-dependent Gaussian evidence with the generative hierarchy. Here image x produces
h1=ReLU(784→32), then h2=ReLU(32→16). Separate linear heads on h1 predict four-coordinate
lower Gaussian evidence, while heads on h2 predict a two-coordinate top posterior.
Explicit top noise samples z2; a 2→16 ReLU conditional network predicts p(z1|z2).
Precision fusion combines that prior with evidence to form q(z1|x,z2), then lower noise samples z1.

The generative model factorizes p(z2)p(z1|z2)p(x|z1). **Only z1 enters the decoder**
4→32 ReLU→784 logits. Top samples affect reconstruction through their learned lower prior
and the fused lower posterior, with no direct top-code or image-feature bypass. This differs
from the spatial hierarchy report, whose decoder explicitly uses both latent groups.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ladder_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
