\caption(Bottom-up evidence and the sampled-top conditional prior meet at precision fusion. Only the lower sampled code reaches the generative decoder.)
\alttext(An image supplies two ReLU features and lower evidence. Top samples produce a learned lower prior, fused with evidence before lower sampling and decoding.)

> Precision fusion by hand

For evidence N(u,exp(v)) and prior N(p,exp(r)), precisions add coordinatewise:

$$
\tau=e^{-v}+e^{-r},\qquad l_q=-\log\tau,\qquad
\mu_q=e^{l_q-v}u+e^{l_q-r}p.
$$
\alttext(The posterior precision is the sum of the evidence and prior precisions. Its mean weights each source by that source's share of total precision.)

Evidence mean2/variance4 and prior mean−1/variance9 give posterior mean14/13 and variance36/13.
Two identical Gaussians halve variance; fusion is not averaging log variances or adding residual
heads. The implementation shifts log precisions by their detached maximum before exponentiating,
retaining all four continuous input paths. It preserves the source operation order and Float32
rounding; no variance clipping is applied. Very large log-scale cancellation is not repaired.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ladder_fusion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  namespace m  = n::models;
  const auto t = n::DType::Float64;
  auto       q = m::LadderPrecisionFusion(
      n::full({1, 1}, 2, t),
      n::full({1, 1}, std::log(4.), t),
      n::full({1, 1}, -1, t),
      n::full({1, 1}, std::log(9.), t));
  if (std::abs(q.mu.item() - 14. / 13) > 1e-14 ||
      std::abs(std::exp(q.log_variance.item()) - 36. / 13) > 1e-14)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "Evidence(2,4) + prior(-1,9): fused mean {:.12f}, variance {:.12f}.\n",
      q.mu.item(),
      std::exp(q.log_variance.item()));
  std::vector<double> logvar, mean, variance;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 40; ++i) {
    double v   = -2 + i * .15;
    auto   out = m::LadderPrecisionFusion(
        n::full({1, 1}, 2, t),
        n::full({1, 1}, v, t),
        n::full({1, 1}, -1, t),
        n::full({1, 1}, std::log(9.), t));
    logvar.push_back(v);
    mean.push_back(out.mu.item());
    variance.push_back(std::exp(out.log_variance.item()));
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(logvar, mean, "fused mean", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(logvar, variance, "fused variance", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Precision fusion / fixed prior mean-1, variance9")
      .x_label("evidence log variance / nats")
      .y_label("fused mean or variance")
      .save_svg("build/ladder_fusion.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Evidence(2,4) + prior(-1,9): fused mean 1.076923076923, variance 2.769230769231.
\image(figures/ladder_fusion.svg)
// result_end

\caption(As evidence becomes less precise, the mean moves toward the prior and posterior variance rises toward the prior variance. Mean and variance are shown as separately labelled quantities.)
\alttext(A falling fused-mean curve and rising variance curve show the effect of increasing evidence log variance under a fixed prior.)

For each supplied top draw, the lower KL is the conditional diagonal-Gaussian expression,
while top KL is to standard normal. The training loss is

$$
\frac1B\sum_b\left[\sum_j(\operatorname{softplus}(a_{bj})-x_{bj}a_{bj})
+K_{1b}+K_{2b}\right],\\
K_{1b}=\frac12\sum_d[(r_d-l_{qd})+e^{l_{qd}-r_d}
+(\mu_{qd}-p_d)^2e^{-r_d}-1],\quad
K_{2b}=\frac12\sum_d[\mu_{2d}^2+e^{l_{2d}}-1-l_{2d}].
$$
\alttext(Pixel NLL and latent KL terms sum their coordinates, then average only images. The conditional lower KL depends on the sampled top code.)

The lower KL changes with sampled z2 because its prior and fused posterior both change. Fixed
multi-draw evaluation averages **all three** terms, not NLL alone. Epsilon has six columns:
four lower draws first, two top draws last. Zero epsilon recursively takes top means then
conditional fused lower means; this is not the marginal posterior predictive mean. There is
no BN, warmup, free bits, annealing or clipping in this compact adaptation.

> Native data preparation and complete explicit fitting

Native offline beta-vae-assets preparation exhausts 2 shapes×3 sizes×7 x×7 y=294 unique binary
28×28 images. Radius=size+2, centre=(3x+5,3y+5); circles/squares use inclusive Euclidean/Chebyshev
radii. Residue(x+2y+size+3shape) mod7 assigns test0, validation1, fit2–6, giving 210/42/42
disjoint combinations. These are tiny structured teaching data, not an IID image benchmark.
Factor indices are saved for provenance but never enter the network or epoch selection.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build/ladder_vae");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
  auto                       arrays = n::load_npz((cache / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  std::set<int>              ids;
  std::set<std::vector<int>> images;
  for (auto& [name, value] : arrays) {
    if (name.ends_with("_images")) {
      for (int b = 0; b < value.size(0); ++b) {
        auto row = n::select(value, 0, b).to_vector<int>();
        if (!images.insert(row).second)
          return 1;
      }
      value = n::cast(value, n::DType::Float32);
    }
    if (name.ends_with("_source_ids"))
      for (int id : value.to_vector<int>())
        if (!ids.insert(id).second)
          return 1;
  }
  if (ids.size() != 294 || images.size() != 294)
    return 1;
  n::save_npz("build/ladder_vae/data.npz", arrays);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "beta_vae/manifest.json",
      "build/ladder_vae/data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print(
      "| split | images | features |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| fit |210|784|\n| validation |42|784|\n| "
      "test |42|784|\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| split | images | features |
|---|---:|---:|
| fit |210|784|
| validation |42|784|
| test |42|784|
// result_end

Seed2503 initializes the 22 trainable leaves. BatchOrder(210,32,2507) gives seven updates per
epoch, including the final 18-image batch, for 21 Adam steps. Learning rate0.003, moments0.9/0.999
and epsilon1e-8 match the source. Fresh training noise banks use seeds2552/2553/2554; fixed four-
draw fit/validation/test banks use2521/2531/2539, with ancestral seed2543. Explicit local
MT19937/Box–Muller Float64 draws and Float32 casts are both saved.

Completed epochs1–3 are eligible. The minimum fixed four-draw validation negative ELBO selects
the checkpoint; test pixels never select it. Evaluation accumulates each Float32 per-case term
in Float64, draw then row, preserving the exact source criterion. Fresh model-only restore
reproduces that score; optimizer-resume state is not saved. The actual gradient and Adam step
remain visible in the full editable program below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& why) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double x, double y, double tolerance, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(x - y) <= tolerance, why);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
nn::Tensor Flatten(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return nn::reshape(t, {t.size(0), 784});
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& key) {
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (k == key)
      return v;
  throw std::runtime_error(key);
}
std::vector<float> Bytes(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return t.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  for (const auto& k : p.names())
    a.emplace_back(k, p.at(k).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      p,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& gs,
    const std::string&,
    const std::string&) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  Require(gs.size() == p.size(), "all22 gradients");
  const auto names = p.names();
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gs.size(); ++i) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (double x : gs[i].to_vector<double>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(x), "finite derivatives");
      norm += x * x;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, "nonzero derivative in each tensor");
    a.emplace_back(names[i], gs[i]);
  }
  return a;
}

VaeNoiseBank LadderNoise(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t samples, std::uint32_t seed) {
  auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({n, 6}, samples, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor LadderNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& bank, std::int64_t k) {
  return nn::select(bank.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors
Evaluate(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& images, const nn::Tensor& noise) {
  nn::NoGradGuard  guard;
  auto             o = nn::models::LadderVariationalAutoencoder(p, Flatten(images), noise);
  nn::NamedTensors out{
      {"evidence_mu", o.evidence_mu},
      {"evidence_lv", o.evidence_lv},
      {"top_mu", o.top_mu},
      {"top_lv", o.top_lv},
      {"top_z", o.top_z},
      {"prior_mu", o.prior_mu},
      {"prior_lv", o.prior_lv},
      {"lower_mu", o.lower_mu},
      {"lower_lv", o.lower_lv},
      {"lower_z", o.lower_z},
      {"probability", o.probability},
      {"nll", o.nll},
      {"kl_lower", o.kl_lower},
      {"kl_top", o.kl_top},
      {"loss", o.loss}};
  for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
    t = t.contiguous();
    for (float v : t.to_vector<float>())
      Require(std::isfinite(v), "all fifteen original Ladder fields finite");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::Tensor Decode(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& code) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::sigmoid(nn::models::GaussianVaeDecode(p, code)).contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors Prior(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& top, const nn::Tensor& noise) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto            o = nn::models::LadderPrior(p, top, noise);
  return {
      {"top_z", o.top_z},
      {"lower_noise", o.lower_noise},
      {"prior_mu", o.prior_mu.contiguous()},
      {"prior_lv", o.prior_lv.contiguous()},
      {"lower_z", o.lower_z.contiguous()},
      {"probability", o.probability.contiguous()}};
}
bool SameBytes(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return a.dtype() == b.dtype() && a.shape() == b.shape() && Bytes(a) == Bytes(b);
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b, int count) {
  auto   x = Bytes(a), y = Bytes(b);
  double result = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < count; ++i)
    result = std::max(result, std::abs(double(x[i]) - y[i]));
  return result;
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& image) {
  return nn::cast(nn::mean(nn::cast(Flatten(image), nn::DType::Float64), {0}), nn::DType::Float32);
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int n) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(row.reshape({1, 784}), {n, 784}).contiguous();
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(Flatten(a), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(Flatten(b), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}
std::vector<BetaFactorData> LoadData(const std::filesystem::path& path) {
  auto                        a = nn::load_npz(path.string());
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> out;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    out.push_back(
        {Find(a, split + "_images"), Find(a, split + "_factors"), Find(a, split + "_source_ids")});
  return out;
}
std::vector<double>
LadderScore(nn::ParameterStore& model, const nn::Tensor& images, const VaeNoiseBank& noise) {
  double             nll = 0, lower = 0, top = 0;
  const std::int64_t n = images.size(0), samples = noise.epsilon.size(0);
  for (std::int64_t k = 0; k < samples; ++k) {
    auto       f = Evaluate(model, images, LadderNoiseAt(noise, k));
    const auto a = Find(f, "nll").to_vector<float>(), b = Find(f, "kl_lower").to_vector<float>(),
               c = Find(f, "kl_top").to_vector<float>();
    for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
      nll += a[i];
      lower += b[i];
      top += c[i];
    }
  }
  const double count = double(n * samples);
  return {nll / count, lower / count, top / count, (nll + lower + top) / count};
}
void Checks(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  const std::vector<float> u{2, -1, .3f, .8f}, v{float(std::log(4)), 0, -.2f, .4f},
      p{-1, 1, .1f, -.4f}, r{float(std::log(9)), float(std::log(4)), .6f, -.3f};
  auto U  = nn::from_vector(u, {2, 2}).requires_grad_(),
       V  = nn::from_vector(v, {2, 2}).requires_grad_(),
       P  = nn::from_vector(p, {2, 2}).requires_grad_(),
       R  = nn::from_vector(r, {2, 2}).requires_grad_();
  auto q  = nn::models::LadderPrecisionFusion(U, V, P, R);
  auto kl = nn::models::ConditionalGaussianKl(q.mu, q.log_variance, P, R);
  auto objective =
      nn::sum(nn::square(q.mu) + nn::square(q.log_variance), {0, 1}) + nn::sum(kl, {0});
  auto       g = nn::grad(objective, {U, V, P, R});
  nn::Tensor extreme_mu, extreme_lv, zero;
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    auto            extreme = nn::models::LadderPrecisionFusion(
        U,
        nn::from_vector(std::vector<float>{-80, 80, 80, -80}, {2, 2}),
        P,
        nn::from_vector(std::vector<float>{80, -80, -80, 80}, {2, 2}));
    extreme_mu = extreme.mu.contiguous();
    extreme_lv = extreme.log_variance.contiguous();
    zero       = nn::models::ConditionalGaussianKl(U, V, U, V).contiguous();
  }
  std::vector<nn::Tensor> out{
      q.mu.detach().contiguous(),
      q.log_variance.detach().contiguous(),
      kl.detach().contiguous(),
      g[0],
      g[1],
      g[2],
      g[3],
      extreme_mu,
      extreme_lv,
      zero};
  for (const auto& t : out)
    for (float x : t.contiguous().to_vector<float>())
      Require(std::isfinite(x), "finite fusion and all gradients");
  for (const auto& t : {g[0], g[1], g[2], g[3]}) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (float x : t.contiguous().to_vector<float>())
      norm += double(x) * x;
    Require(norm > 0, "fusion derivatives include evidence AND prior mean/logvariance");
  }
  const auto mu = out[0].to_vector<float>(), lv = out[1].to_vector<float>(),
             z = out[9].to_vector<float>();
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    const double a = std::exp(-double(v[i])), b = std::exp(-double(r[i]));
    Near(mu[i], (a * u[i] + b * p[i]) / (a + b), 3e-7, "known precision weighted mean");
    Near(lv[i], -std::log(a + b), 3e-7, "known harmonic posterior variance");
  }
  for (int b = 0; b < 2; ++b)
    Near(z[b], 0, 0, "conditional KL(q||q) exactly zero");
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "fusion_algebra.npz").string(),
      {{"evidence_mu", U.detach()},
       {"evidence_lv", V.detach()},
       {"prior_mu", P.detach()},
       {"prior_lv", R.detach()},
       {"mu", out[0]},
       {"lv", out[1]},
       {"kl", out[2]},
       {"du", out[3]},
       {"dv", out[4]},
       {"dp", out[5]},
       {"dr", out[6]},
       {"extreme_mu", out[7]},
       {"extreme_lv", out[8]}});
  std::cout << "precision fusion/evidence+prior gradients/conditional KL zero/extreme stable "
               "precisions passed"
            << std::endl;
}

nn::Tensor Columns(const nn::Tensor& x, std::int64_t begin, std::int64_t end) {
  return nn::slice_axis(x, 1, begin, end).contiguous();
}

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  auto pools = LoadData(data);
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  Checks(root);
  std::vector<VaeNoiseBank> noise{
      LadderNoise(210, 4, 2521), LadderNoise(42, 4, 2531), LadderNoise(42, 4, 2539)},
      training;
  auto             prior_noise = LadderNoise(20, 1, 2543);
  nn::NamedTensors fixed{
      {"prior_standard", prior_noise.standard}, {"prior_epsilon", prior_noise.epsilon}};
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_standard", noise[split].standard);
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_epsilon", noise[split].epsilon);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), fixed);
  for (int e = 1; e <= epochs; ++e) {
    training.push_back(LadderNoise(210, 1, 2551 + e));
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(e) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", training.back().standard}, {"epsilon", training.back().epsilon}});
  }
  nn::ParameterStore model(2503);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::LadderVariationalAutoencoder(model, nn::zeros({1, 784}), nn::zeros({1, 6}));
  }
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  if (!init.empty())
    model.load(init);
  Require(model.size() == 22 && model.count() == 52196, "two-level ladder parameter census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model));
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 2507);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\ttrain_preupdate_negative_elbo\tvalidation_nll\tvalidation_lower_"
             "kl\tvalidation_top_kl\t"
             "validation_negative_elbo\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, step = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    order.begin_epoch();
    double sum     = 0;
    int    seen    = 0;
    auto   epsilon = LadderNoiseAt(training[epoch - 1], 0);
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), e = nn::take_rows(epsilon, rows);
      if (step == 0) {
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"images", x}, {"epsilon", e}});
        auto g = CheckGradients(
            model,
            nn::grad(
                nn::models::LadderVariationalAutoencoder(model, Flatten(x), e).loss,
                model.parameters()),
            "all ladder gradients finite",
            "all22tensors receive gradients");
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_gradients.npz").string(), g);
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), Evaluate(model, x, e));
      }
      auto train = nn::models::LadderVariationalAutoencoder(model, Flatten(x), e);
      sum += double(rows.size()) * train.loss.item<float>();
      optimizer.step(nn::grad(train.loss, model.parameters()));
      seen += int(rows.size());
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << step << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      if (step == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model));
      ++step;
    }
    Require(seen == 210, "all210fitting cases once per epoch");
    auto score = LadderScore(model, pools[1].images, noise[1]);
    history << epoch << '\t' << sum / seen;
    for (auto value : score)
      history << '\t' << value;
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), Arrays(model));
    if (score[3] < best) {
      best     = score[3];
      selected = epoch;
      model.save(best_path); // four-sample validation ELBO selects checkpoint
    }
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();

  nn::ParameterStore deployed(2503);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::LadderVariationalAutoencoder(deployed, nn::zeros({1, 784}), nn::zeros({1, 6}));
  }
  deployed.load(best_path); // fresh ladder model-only restore
  Near(
      LadderScore(deployed, pools[1].images, noise[1])[3],
      best,
      1e-8,
      "fresh selected validation score");
  const auto       before = Snapshot(deployed);
  nn::NamedTensors output;
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::int64_t n      = pools[split].images.size(0);
    const std::string  name   = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    auto               greedy = Evaluate(deployed, pools[split].images, nn::zeros({n, 6}));
    Require(
        SameBytes(Find(greedy, "lower_z"), Find(greedy, "lower_mu")) &&
            SameBytes(Find(greedy, "top_z"), Find(greedy, "top_mu")),
        "both zero-noise samples equal their recursive means");
    for (const auto& [key, value] : greedy)
      output.emplace_back(name + "_greedy_" + key, value);
    for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k) {
      auto f = Evaluate(deployed, pools[split].images, LadderNoiseAt(noise[split], k));
      for (const auto& [key, value] : f)
        output.emplace_back(name + "_draw" + std::to_string(k) + "_" + key, value);
    }
  }
  auto test   = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, LadderNoiseAt(noise[2], 0)),
       repeat = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, LadderNoiseAt(noise[2], 0));
  Require(
      SameBytes(Find(test, "probability"), Find(repeat, "probability")) &&
          SameBytes(Find(test, "probability"), Decode(deployed, Find(test, "lower_z"))),
      "repeat and target-free lower latent decode BITEXACT");
  auto single = Evaluate(
      deployed,
      nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0}),
      nn::take_rows(LadderNoiseAt(noise[2], 0), {0}));
  const double parity = MaxAbsDiff(Find(single, "probability"), Find(test, "probability"), 784);
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "single/batch parity");
  std::vector<float> lower(42 * 6, 0.f), upper(42 * 6, 0.f);
  for (int b = 0; b < 42; ++b) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j)
      lower[b * 6 + j] = .5f;
    for (int j = 4; j < 6; ++j)
      upper[b * 6 + j] = .5f;
  }
  auto base = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, nn::zeros({42, 6})),
       low  = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, nn::from_vector(lower, {42, 6})),
       top  = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, nn::from_vector(upper, {42, 6}));
  Require(
      SameBytes(Find(base, "lower_mu"), Find(low, "lower_mu")) &&
          SameBytes(Find(base, "prior_mu"), Find(low, "prior_mu")) &&
          MaxAbsDiff(Find(base, "lower_z"), Find(low, "lower_z"), 42 * 4) > 1e-4,
      "lower noise changes sample only,not hierarchy heads");
  const double prior_effect  = MaxAbsDiff(Find(base, "prior_mu"), Find(top, "prior_mu"), 42 * 4),
               fusion_effect = MaxAbsDiff(Find(base, "lower_mu"), Find(top, "lower_mu"), 42 * 4);
  Require(
      prior_effect > 1e-5 && fusion_effect > 1e-5,
      "top noise changes conditional prior AND fused lower posterior");
  nn::save_npz((root / "top_noise_intervention.npz").string(), top);
  nn::save_npz((root / "lower_noise_intervention.npz").string(), low);
  auto prior_bank = LadderNoiseAt(prior_noise, 0);
  auto prior      = Prior(deployed, Columns(prior_bank, 4, 6), Columns(prior_bank, 0, 4));
  Require(
      SameBytes(Find(prior, "probability"), Decode(deployed, Find(prior, "lower_z"))),
      "ancestral hierarchical sample decodes exactly");
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), prior);
  Require(before == Snapshot(deployed), "all inference/prior/intervention calls immutable");
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(deployed));
  auto          score    = LadderScore(deployed, pools[2].images, noise[2]);
  const double  mse      = Mse(Find(output, "test_greedy_probability"), pools[2].images);
  auto          mean     = Constant(PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const double  mean_mse = Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":52196,\"tensors\":22,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << step
       << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected << ",\"mc_samples\":4,\"test_nll\":" << score[0]
       << ",\"test_lower_kl\":" << score[1] << ",\"test_top_kl\":" << score[2]
       << ",\"test_negative_elbo\":" << score[3] << ",\"greedy_decode_test_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"fit_mean_test_mse\":" << mean_mse << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"top_noise_prior_mu_max_effect\":" << prior_effect
       << ",\"top_noise_fused_mu_max_effect\":" << fusion_effect
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete Ladder evidence");
  std::print(
      "| selected epoch | test NLL | lower KL | top KL | negative ELBO | greedy MSE | fit-mean MSE "
      "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | "
      "{:.9f} |\n",
      selected,
      score[0],
      score[1],
      score[2],
      score[3],
      mse,
      mean_mse);
  std::print(
      "Top-noise prior-mean effect {:.9f}; fused-mean effect {:.9f}.\n",
      prior_effect,
      fusion_effect);
}
int main() {
  Run("build/ladder_vae/data.npz", "build/ladder_vae", 3, "");
}
```
