> Validation selection and honest controls

The fixed validation criterion decreases over the three completed epochs, selecting epoch3.
The test score decomposes into NLL234.154285, lower KL7.508567 and top KL4.866975, totaling
246.529827. Greedy MSE0.073146 is worse than fitting mean0.048548. The run does not establish
useful reconstruction, a semantic hierarchy or disentanglement. Top-noise intervention changes
prior means by0.469194 and fused means by0.593488; that demonstrates dependence, not meaning.
Lower noise leaves those heads fixed and changes only lower samples/decoding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ladder_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/ladder_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> epoch, nll, lower, top, total;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    std::istringstream row(line);
    double             e, train, a, b, c, d;
    row >> e >> train >> a >> b >> c >> d;
    if (!row)
      return 1;
    epoch.push_back(e);
    nll.push_back(a);
    lower.push_back(b);
    top.push_back(c);
    total.push_back(d);
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(epoch, nll, "NLL", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(epoch, total, "NLL + lower/top KL", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Fixed four-draw validation")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/ladder_validation.svg");
}
