> Unfiltered reconstruction and ancestral sampling

Ten evenly spaced test indices floor(k×41/9) are shown without filtering. Rows contain the
original, recursive zero-noise reconstruction, one posterior-draw probability image and the
fitting-only mean. The common grayscale range is[0,1]. The prior gallery uses all twenty
prescribed independent top/lower draws: sample z2~N(0,I), then z1~p(z1|z2), then decode z1.
There is no image or encoder input to this ancestral path. Both galleries show probabilities,
not Bernoulli pixel samples; recursive means are not marginal predictive means.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ladder_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto find   = [](const n::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& key) {
    for (const auto& [k, t] : a)
      if (k == key)
        return t;
    throw std::runtime_error(key);
  };
  auto data = n::load_npz("build/ladder_vae/data.npz"),
       out  = n::load_npz("build/ladder_vae/outputs.npz");
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i)
    rows.push_back(i * 41 / 9);
  auto                   mean = n::mean(find(data, "fit_images").reshape({210, 784}), {0}, true);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
  for (const auto& x : std::vector<n::Tensor>{
           find(data, "test_images"),
           find(out, "test_greedy_probability"),
           find(out, "test_draw0_probability"),
           n::broadcast_to(mean, {42, 784})})
    panels.push_back(n::take_rows(x, rows).reshape({10, 28, 28, 1}));
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(panels, 0), "build/ladder_reconstructions.png", 10, 0, 1, 4, 220. / 255, 3);
}
