> Reproduction evidence and binding boundary

All20 source NPZ archives are compared by dtype, shape and every value byte: fusion algebra,
initial/first-update/every-epoch/selected weights, all first derivatives, noise banks, fifteen
original forward fields for each greedy/four-draw pool evaluation, both noise interventions
and all six ancestral endpoints. Full histories and batch/source orders match exactly.
The optional NumPy oracle independently checks all first parameter derivatives, exact first
Adam update, all four fusion partials, Gaussian banks, every saved hierarchy/decoder endpoint
and every eligible four-draw validation criterion. It does not fit or prepare/download data.

```
python3 scripts/check_ladder_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/ladder_vae --json build/nn-report-conversion/ladder_vae/oracle.json
```

Native functions are LadderPrecisionFusion, LadderPrior and LadderVariationalAutoencoder,
reusing ConditionalGaussianKl and GaussianVaeDecode. The full native result additionally
owns logits, for sixteen fields; the source archive protocol preserves its original fifteen.
Python/R expose the same operations. Tests retain fusion/ancestral/full fields through parent
collection, verify Float64 input/noise/prior paths and make caller-owned Adam explicit. This
API/report conversion does not mark unfinished independent Python/R experiment loops as ports.
